      "comments": "https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=49936575",
      "why_read": "Learn how DwarfStar 4 enables local execution of massive mixture-of-experts models through asymmetric quantization and disk-persisted KV caching. This provides a clear architectural model for running frontier models efficiently on consumer hardware.",
      "authors": [
        "fibo"
      ],
      "image": "/infographics/04-hn-49936575.jpg",
      "content": "Salvatore Sanfilippo has released DwarfStar 4, a minimalist C inference engine engineered to run massive frontier mixture-of-experts models locally on consumer workstations.\n\nInstead of uniform weight reduction across billions of parameters, ds4 applies asymmetric two-bit quantization specifically to the routed experts while preserving full precision on critical shared paths. This architecture allows models like DeepSeek V4 Flash to fit within high-memory machines without crippling reasoning fidelity.\n\nThe KV cache architecture is equally pragmatic. Prompts are hashed via SHA1 and cached directly to disk, turning prefix computation into a fast SSD lookup that survives server restarts. A single resident binary exposes a CLI, HTTP endpoints, and persistent coding agent harnesses over the shared state.\n\nHigh-throughput local inference does not require massive distributed clusters when you optimize memory layouts at the metal."
    },
